# WP-QUALITY-HITCH (11-22): the 4.7 s "worst frame" the profiler showed right after the High -> Cinematic switch in
# CINEMATIC-LOD. Measured, not guessed: "[Control] long frame N: X ms" names every frame over 250 ms with its
# serial; `frames 60` + `profile-dump` bracket the 60 frames after the switch ([Hitch] lines, slowest first); the
# shot line "[Control] wrote the presented frame ... on the frame X ms, PNG encode + write on a worker Y ms" splits
# a window shot's cost. Scene and camera as CINEMATIC-LOD (the crowd 30-300 m behind the origin figure).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_FAR11_SkinnedCrowd.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Когда run Mode "Select mode"
Когда run Action "Play from Here"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 90
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,0,30000
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,0,-1
Когда advance 2
Когда frames 60
Когда profile-dump
Тогда 0_before_switch High at 300 m, the crowd at the horizon; log: the [Hitch] of the 60 frames before (the reference)
Когда run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance Cinematic"
Когда frames 60
Когда profile-dump
Тогда 1_after_switch Cinematic, same view: the crowd at the horizon present; log: no "[Control] long frame" between the switch and this shot, the 60 frames after the switch with their [Hitch] ms (< 250 ms), this shot's own on-the-frame ms
Когда frames 30
Тогда 2_next_shot a second shot after 30 frames: the frame after 1_after_switch's shot is not a long frame (the PNG went to a worker)
Когда run Action "Stop"
